  "title": "Never Stop Driving #192: When Will We Have Our Own Goodwood Hill Climb?",
  "summary": "This past weekend, some 200,000 folks attended the annual Goodwood Festival of Speed (FOS) in the U.K. There they watched—and heard—hundreds of cars race up the hill-climb course that cuts, for just over a mile, through the Goodwood estate. When the Duke of Richmond, Charles Gordon-Lennox, started the hill climb on his family’s ancestral estate […]",
